// The **Markdown** screen's two panes, and the point of this file is that there
// are only two nodes in it that matter.
//
// `text-area` writes `md.source` through an action; `markdown-view` reads the
// same property with `bind=`. Nothing watches the editor, diffs the text or
// schedules a re-render: the element holding the preview is subscribed to the
// property, a keystroke marks it for rebuild, and the next frame is the parsed
// document (ADR-0062, ADR-0296). A live preview is a binding.
//
// `markdown-view` is also not this application's widget and this document never
// says where it comes from. `goldberry-html` is on the module path, its catalog
// declares the node name, and the inflater finds it through a `uses` — ADR-0131's
// promise about a second widget module, exercised rather than asserted.
//
// A `split-pane` at the root rather than a masonry: this screen is one thing
// divided, not a wall of cards, and `Screen` puts it in a tab that is deliberately
// **not** scrolled — the preview owns a viewport, and §2.4 bans nested same-axis
// scrollers.
split-pane id="markdown-split" position=0.5 first-min=240 second-min=240 {
    column id="markdown-editor" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Markdown — type here"
        // `fill=#true` is the editor half of §4's `text-area`: the height comes
        // from this pane rather than from the text, and the document scrolls
        // inside it (ADR-0296). Without it the area is `max-rows` tall and the
        // rest of the side is empty.
        //
        // `class="mono"` and nothing else besides. What this is *not* is a code
        // editor with line numbers and highlighting -- that is `goldberry-code`,
        // and it is a module that does not exist (book/src/TODO.md).
        text-area id="markdown-source" class="mono" bind="md.source" change="md.set-source" fill=#true
    }
    column id="markdown-preview" class="markdown-pane" {
        text class="caption" "Rendered — this side follows"
        // What the last pressed link or ticked box reported. The preview is not a
        // picture of a document: `link=` and `wikilink=` name valued actions that are
        // handed a destination, and `task=` is handed the **ordinal** of the box --
        // which `Markdown.toggleTask` turns into one changed character of the source
        // on the left (ADR-0300).
        text id="markdown-followed" class="caption" bind="md.followed"
        scroll {
            markdown-view id="markdown-rendered" bind="md.source" \
                link="md.follow" wikilink="md.open-wiki" task="md.toggle-task" images="app.assets"
        }
    }
}
